<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψᾰκάς</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 and later (cf. Moer.<i><span class="en">
			p.419
		</span></i> P.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεκάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ἡ</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drop of rain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν μὲν κατὰ μικρὰ φέρηται, ψακάδες,
					ὅταν δὲ κατὰ μείζω μόρια, ὑετὸς καλεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					347a11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				348a7
			</span></i>, al.; <i>particle,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				373b16
			</span></i>: mostly collect., <i>drizzle,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψακὰς δὲ λήγει,</span> i. e. heavy rain
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβρος</span>) is coming, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1534
			</span></i> (lyr.); opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑετοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				5.4
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕσθησαν αἱ Θῆβαι ψακάδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.10
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>rain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ στέγῃ πυκνῆς ἀκοῦσαι ψακάδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					636
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				856
			</span></i>; so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεκάς</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				2.3.1
			</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεκάδες</span>”
				<i>showers,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					17(1).37
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοίνισσα ψακάς</span>
			<i>a shower</i> of blood, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				106
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλλει μ᾽ ἐρεμνῇ ψακάδι φοινίας
					δρόσου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1390
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βρομίου ψακάδεσσι,</span> i. e.
				<i>drops</i> of wine, <i><span class="en">
				Critias
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Comic name
			for <i>a sputterer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1150
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			s.v.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph. of solids,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργυρίου μηδὲ ψακάς</span> not a
				<i>drop</i> of money, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				121
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ψάμμου] ψεκάς</span>
			<i>grains</i> of sand, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.145
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψακάς</span> prob. by
			assimilation from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεκάς.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
